{"kind":"request","text":"GS-1: a shorter gate and a lighter record. Hugh approved the three\nparts on 14 November (f45b355a).\n\nThe facts, from the C1 gate of 14 November, one observed run. The\ngate script took 1094 s, and its test step took 1067 s: Native 854 s,\nNode 125 s, Plain 84 s. From START to END the run took 1646 s, so\nthe supervisor and the seal added 552 s. Sixteen Native cases took\nmore than 10 s each and 656 s together. One case took 293 s:\n`fixed-slot-membership.scope.test.ts`, with a room of 2000 members.\n\nWork, in one head. Split part C into its own head if its audit\nholds parts A and B for more than one hour.\n\n## Part A. The documents state the lighter record\n\n1. `docs/evidence-filing.md` states the record of f45b355a section\n   3: one log in a new directory under `~/play/artroom-evidence/`,\n   and its SHA-256 in the note's evidence table. Remove the\n   `SHA256SUMS` file, the read-only step and the committed\n   manifest from \"File the evidence\", \"Review a change\" and \"The\n   implementation note and its evidence\".\n2. The reviewer's check becomes: the log exists at the path, its\n   SHA-256 equals the note's, its first lines name the reviewed\n   head and tree with 0 changed files, and its last line says the\n   gate passed.\n3. The section on the focused plan says that the tool is optional\n   and that no head owes a focused run.\n4. The gate's `notes` step stops its warning about paths under\n   `notes/implementation/evidence/`, or the step goes if nothing\n   else uses it. Manifests in the tree stay.\n5. `docs/testing.md` agrees with the above.\n\n## Part B. A notes-only head skips the test step\n\n1. When each path that differs from the merge base is under\n   `notes/`, the gate skips its test step and prints one line that\n   says so. Its other steps run.\n2. Name each test that reads a file under `notes/`. If one exists,\n   the notes-only gate still runs that test file.\n3. One test of the selection: a notes-only change, a change under\n   `docs/`, and a mixed change. Only the first skips.\n\n## Part C. The slow Native cases move to the scale tier\n\n1. List each Native case over 10 s in the R2 Grow gate log\n   (`~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-14-r2-grow-gate-attempt1`),\n   with its time.\n2. For each case, state in the note what it shows and which source\n   paths it protects. Where a small configured limit shows the same\n   rule, keep that small case in the ordinary tier, as\n   `docs/testing.md` says for a bound.\n3. Move each listed case to the scale tier. Remove no case.\n4. Add the protected source paths to the scale selection, so that\n   a change to one of them runs the scale tier in the gate.\n5. `docs/testing-reference.md` lists the moved cases.\n6. The note states the wall time of the gate's Native step before\n   and after, each from one observed run.\n\nA scale run on main once each sprint day keeps the moved cases\nhonest. The builder starts it when the slot is idle and reports the\nresult in one act.\n\nOrder: GS-1 takes the slot after the combined head.","body":{"conditions":"docs/evidence-filing.md and docs/testing.md state the record of f45b355a section 3. A head that changes only paths under notes/ skips the gate's test step, and a test covers the selection. Each Native case over 10 s is in the scale tier with its protected paths in the scale selection, and the note lists each moved case with what it shows. The note states the Native step wall time before and after. The gate passes and the checker reviews the head.","target_head":"189cf7b64a1501b307b9c73e96ee83641c3bd2de","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}